From kimai-cTYGs6MY1n4q5t9Oc1ygMg at public.gmane.org  Sat Feb 12 16:47:37 2011
From: kimai-cTYGs6MY1n4q5t9Oc1ygMg at public.gmane.org (Kosuke Imai)
Date: Sat, 12 Feb 2011 11:47:37 -0500
Subject: Re: Simulate second difference
In-Reply-To: <AANLkTimQ9dd9BY6cfCeGZUDSN8R8k=E6Ohs9u41cJJse@mail.gmail.com>
References: <AANLkTimQ9dd9BY6cfCeGZUDSN8R8k=E6Ohs9u41cJJse@mail.gmail.com>
Message-ID: <C4AEEA5F-761B-46DB-8EE3-3A750DBF06D1@Princeton.Edu>

You can trick Zelig to do this.  Set the random seed to the same number each time you run sim(); e.g., set.seed(12345)  Then, you can do what you suggest below.  This way, the same draws of parameters will be used to get the uncertainty estimates correctly. 

Kosuke

Department of Politics
Princeton University
http://imai.princeton.edu

